ts. No analytics. No answers sent to a server. Shared answers are visible in the URL.</p></aside></div></section>}
      {view==='methodology' && <section className="tool-section methodology"><span className="eyebrow">SHOWING OUR WORK</span><h2>A comparison you can check.</h2><p className="section-intro">This project describes voter-guide recommendations. It does not endorse candidates, measures, or political groups.</p><div className="method-layout"><article><h3>What the numbers mean</h3><p>For a measure, the split score is the smaller of the Yes and No counts divided by all Yes / No positions. A 50% split means an even divide. Missing recommendations and explicit no-position statements do not enter the denominator.</p><p>For a race, the leader is the candidate with the most guide endorsements. Each guide contributes at most one endorsement per candidate. The split is the share of guides that back none of the tied leaders. A multi-candidate selection counts as supporting a leader if that person is in the set. When all candidates tie, the split can be 0%; the individual cells still show their different selections.</p><p>Most split: at least 40%. Contested: at least 20% and below 40%. Mostly agreed: below 20%. Buckets use exact values before rounding. All scores use the full snapshot, regardless of hidden columns.</p><h3>How the data is collected</h3><p>The scraper reads server-rendered tables at <a href="https://sfendorsements.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SF Endorsements</a> and parses supported direct guide pages. Direct positions take precedence. Each cell records its source URL, retrieval time, collection method, and confidence. An asterisk marks aggregator-only positions that need direct review.</p><p>Raw responses are cached, requests identify the scraper, and robots rules are checked. A manual override file permits sourced corrections. Daily refreshes open review pull requests rather than publishing automatically.</p><h3>What to keep in mind</h3><p>Political camps are editorial groupings supplied for this comparison, not verified self-descriptions. Organizations can disagree with others in their group. Candidate lists contain names discovered in endorsements and may not include everyone on the ballot. Candidate order in aggregator cells is unverified. Multi-seat slates are sets, not rankings.</p><p>Judicial retention questions are treated as Yes / No measures. House District 15 is excluded because it is outside San Francisco. Descriptions are source labels rather than independent policy analyses. Read the linked guide and official ballot materials for details.</p><p>No rationales are inferred from advocacy text. A missing recommendation means the scraper did not find one; it does not establish neutrality. A dash means the guide explicitly took no position.</p><h3>Pairwise and camp agreement</h3><p>Guide agreement compares only shared, substantive positions. Measure positions must match; race candidate sets must match exactly. Verified rankings also require matching order. Camp agreement pools all within-camp guide pairs, weighted by the number of shared contests.</p><div className="camp-stats">{Object.entries(derived.camps).map(([name,metric])=><div key={name}><span>{name}<small>{metric.count} shared guide-pair contests</small></span><b>{percent(metric.score)}</b></div>)}</div><h3>Source access notes</h3><ul className="source-notes">{data.source_issues.map((issue,i)=><li key={i}>{issue}</li>)}</ul><a className="outline-button" href={data.report_error_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Report a data error <Icon name="external" size={15}/></a></article><aside><h3>The source shelf</h3><p>{data.guides.length} guides. Every position has a citation.</p>{data.guides.map(g=>{const count=data.positions.filter(p=>p.guide_id===g.id && hasPosition(p)).length;const direct=data.positions.filter(p=>p.guide_id===g.id && p.collection==='direct').length;return <a className="source-card" key={g.id} href={g.url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"><div><b>{g.name}</b><Icon name="external" size={14}/></div><small>{g.camp}</small><p>{count} positions · {direct} direct cells</p><span>{g.inspection.status==='unavailable'?'Direct page unavailable; aggregator used':direct?'Direct + aggregator sources':'Aggregator-only positions'}</span></a>;})}</aside></div></section>}
      <section className="bottom-note"><span className="eyebrow">MAKE UP YOUR OWN MIND</span><p>Agreement is a starting point.<br/><b>The reasoning is in the sources.</b></p><button onClick={()=>setView('methodology')}>Explore the sources <Icon name="arrow"/></button></section>
    </main>
    <footer><a className="footer-brand" href="?">SF BALLOT ATLAS <span>↗</span></a><span>An independent look at the November 2026 ballot.</span><a href={data.report_error_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Report an error ↗</a></footer>
    <dialog ref={dialog} onCancel={()=>setSelected(null)} onClick={e=>{if(e.target===dialog.current)setSelected(null);}} aria-labelledby="contest-title" className="contest-dialog">{selected&&<div className="drawer-content"><button className="close-dialog" onClick={()=>setSelected(null)} aria-label="Close contest details"><Icon name="close"/></button><span className="eyebrow">{selected.level} · {selected.kind==='race'?'Candidate race':'Ballot measure'}</span><h2 id="contest-title">{selected.name}</h2><p className="drawer-description">{selected.full_title}</p><a className="text-link" href={selected.description_source_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Title source <Icon name="external" size={13}/></a><div className="drawer-split"><strong>{percent(splits[selected.id].score)}</strong><div><b>{splits[selected.id].bucket}</b><p>{splits[selected.id].count-splits[selected.id].majority} of {splits[selected.id].count} guides with a position differ from the leader.</p></div></div><div className="topic-tags">{selected.topics.map(t=><span key={t}>{t}</span>)}</div>{selected.kind==='race'&&<section className="candidates"><h3>Discovered candidate names</h3><p>This list comes from endorsements and may not be the complete ballot.</p><ul>{selected.candidates.map(c=><li key={c.id}>{c.name}</li>)}</ul></section>}<h3 className="guide-positions-title">What each guide says</h3>{camps.map(group=><section className="drawer-camp" key={group}><h4>{group}</h4>{data.guides.filter(g=>g.camp===group).map(g=>{const p=pos(g.id,selected.id);return <div key={g.id} className={'drawer-position '+(focusedGuide===g.id?'highlighted':'')}><span className={'key '+cellClass(p,selected)}>{symbol(p,selected)}</span><div><b>{g.name}</b><p>{choice(p,selected)}</p>{p.selection_type && p.selection_type!=='single'&&<small>{p.selection_type==='ranked'?'Ranked in source order':p.selection_type==='unordered slate'?'Multi-seat slate; unordered':'Multiple names; ranking order unverified'}</small>}{p.rationale&&<p>{p.rationale}</p>}<small>{p.confidence==='low'?'Aggregator-only · needs direct review':p.collection==='direct'?'Direct source':'No position located'} · Retrieved {new Date(p.retrieved_at).toLocaleDateString('en-US',{month:'short',day:'numeric'})}</small>{p.review_note&&<small className="review-note">{p.review_note}</small>}</div><a href={p.source_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label={`${g.name} source for ${selected.name}`}>Source <Icon name="external" size={13}/></a></div>;})}</section>)}<a className="text-link" href={data.report_error_url} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Report an error with this contest ↗</a></div>}</dialog>
